## Conversation
The user asked for an end-to-end validated DFlash2 PR that is faithful to the public serving contracts. The conversion audit found that missing checkpoint weights only produced warnings and that the vocabulary-pruning path was both broken and unsafe for DFlash2 selector token IDs.

## Actions
Made model state loading strict so conversion fails on missing or unexpected tensors. Parsed the draft configuration before checkpoint loading and rejected DFlash2 vocabulary pruning before loading checkpoint or dataset data. Corrected the stale generic pruning call to the one-argument export helper. Ran Ruff format check, Ruff check, and git diff --check. Added no tests or documentation.

## Errors & Mistakes
The original PR used strict=False and logged key mismatches, which could emit a serving artifact from an incomplete checkpoint. Its pruning path passed a stale second argument to _prepare_export_tensors and failed with TypeError only after expensive work.

## Dead Ends
Extending generic vocabulary remapping to DFlash2 was rejected because the candidate selector owns two full target-vocabulary codebooks. Pruning only the language-model head and adding t2d/d2t mappings would leave selector token IDs inconsistent.

## Hints for Future Agents
Convert the full-vocabulary Qwen3-8B DCP without --prune-vocab, --target-model-path, or --vllm. The DCP contains the frozen target embedding for strict reconstruction; state_dict_for_serving removes that training-only tensor before writing the canonical artifact.

## Codebase Discoveries
A one-step run writes iter_0000002 because checkpoint.save increments the completed step. The exact conversion command should point at that iteration root and use torchspec/config/dflash2_draft_config.json with bfloat16 output.

## Open Questions
Strict conversion still needs live proof against the actual FULL_SHARD DCP and a serving engine load. Generic vocabulary pruning was source-corrected but is outside this PR's requested DFlash2 validation and has not been exercised.
